From eac5738fbf050b1ccffc69a888f5ee1a794fc19d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tillmann Severin <tillmann.severin@mailbox.org>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:20:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 24/24] net: hix5hd2_gmac: do not claim TSO on the Hi3798MV200

The Hi3798MV200 GMAC was matched as a GEMAC_V2 part, which sets
HW_CAP_TSO and so makes the driver advertise NETIF_F_SG and send
fragmented skbs through the scatter-gather descriptor format.

That controller does not implement scatter-gather.  The version field in
bits [29:28] of CRF_MIN_PACKET reads 0, VER_NO_TSO, where the
scatter-gather and TSO capable variants read 2 and 3 respectively.

The effect was subtle because only skbs carrying fragments take the
scatter-gather path.  ICMP and small UDP datagrams are linear and were
transmitted fine, as was the TCP handshake, since SYN and ACK carry no
payload.  TCP data however is placed in page fragments whenever
NETIF_F_SG is advertised, so every data segment was built in a
descriptor format the hardware does not understand and was never put on
the wire.  A connection would establish and then stall forever.

Match the controller as GEMAC_V1 so that only the four word descriptor
capability remains.  The driver then uses the full frame descriptor for
every skb and the stack linearises fragmented ones.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/hisilicon/hix5hd2_gmac.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/hisilicon/hix5hd2_gmac.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/hisilicon/hix5hd2_gmac.c
index 29330bffd709..7327f2ccd639 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/hisilicon/hix5hd2_gmac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/hisilicon/hix5hd2_gmac.c
@@ -1351,8 +1351,13 @@ static const struct of_device_id hix5hd2_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "hisilicon,hisi-gmac-v2", .data = (void *)GEMAC_V2 },
 	{ .compatible = "hisilicon,hix5hd2-gmac", .data = (void *)GEMAC_V1 },
 	{ .compatible = "hisilicon,hi3798cv200-gmac", .data = (void *)GEMAC_V2 },
+	/*
+	 * The Hi3798MV200 GMAC reports VER_NO_TSO in the version field of
+	 * CRF_MIN_PACKET, so it implements neither TSO nor the scatter-gather
+	 * descriptor format.  It only supports the four word descriptor layout.
+	 */
 	{ .compatible = "hisilicon,hi3798mv200-gmac",
-	  .data = (void *)(GEMAC_V2 | HW_CAP_DESC_4WORD) },
+	  .data = (void *)(GEMAC_V1 | HW_CAP_DESC_4WORD) },
 	{ .compatible = "hisilicon,hi3516a-gmac", .data = (void *)GEMAC_V2 },
 	{},
 };
